{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3079","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3079","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3079\",\"parent_revision\":\"12f451610701cc8c3c1891ea3cc56ad078ef84f3f96bfc4cc3a2dfa761dc4766\",\"root_revision\":\"12f451610701cc8c3c1891ea3cc56ad078ef84f3f96bfc4cc3a2dfa761dc4766\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nR8's control set (#3062) needs two capabilities beyond a passive hash-mismatch check on read,\\nper ADR-3075-2:\\n\\n1. **Recoverable staleness.** A control-set entry stores the command that produced it (source,\\n   scope, parameters) alongside its content identity. A stale-identifier request re-runs\\n   Collection and Generation via that stored command and serves against the new identity,\\n   instead of erroring and forcing the caller to reconstruct its original request.\\n2. **Write-triggered invalidation.** Every write path that can modify a source this contract\\n   reads from invalidates the control-set entries generated from what it touched, as a side\\n   effect of the write \u2014 not only discovered lazily when a later read happens to hit a\\n   mismatched hash.\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nBlocked on #3062 landing first \u2014 this extends the control set #3062 builds; there is nothing\\nto index or invalidate until it exists.\\n\\nSee ADR-3075-2 (`plugins/development-harness/docs/adrs/`) for the full reasoning.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] The control set indexes entries by the source(s) they were generated from, so a write can\\n      find what to invalidate without scanning every entry\\n- [ ] A stale-identifier request requeries via the entry's stored command and returns fresh\\n      content with a new identity, rather than an error requiring the caller to restart\\n- [ ] Every write path bound by the contract's Scope (item updates, section writes, artifact\\n      registration, task/plan state changes) invalidates matching control-set entries as a\\n      side effect of the write\\n- [ ] A write to content with no corresponding cache entry is a no-op, not an error\\n</div>\\n\\n## Why This Is Its Own Issue Not Part Of 3062\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n#3062 scopes the read-path identity/pagination contract. This issue is the write-side\\nintegration surface: every mutation path in the plugin (item updates, section writes, artifact\\nregistration, task and plan state changes) needs to call into the control set's invalidation\\nhook. That is materially more surface area than #3062's read-path scope and touches code\\n#3057-#3059 do not.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"254356adb030a70c4fe2f35c08078bec51d01486282efd75f346932b0778374c\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPvb6Qw\"}"}